    "problem_statement": "Ticking time goes backwards instead of forward\n\nWhen using `freeze_time` with `tick=True`, the time appears to be going backwards instead of forward. This affects all time-related functions including `datetime.now()`, `date.today()`, and `time.time()`.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport time\nimport datetime\nfrom freezegun import freeze_time\n\n# This should show time moving forward, but it goes backward\nwith freeze_time('Jan 14th, 2012', tick=True):\n    start_time = datetime.datetime.now()\n    time.sleep(0.001)  # Sleep a tiny bit\n    end_time = datetime.datetime.now()\n    print(f\"Start: {start_time}\")\n    print(f\"End: {end_time}\")\n    print(f\"Time moved forward: {end_time > start_time}\")  # Should be True, but is False\n```\n\nThe expected behavior is that `end_time` should be greater than `start_time` since real time has passed, but instead the time appears to be moving backwards."
  },
